WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.970
-My first guest is an Emmy- and
Golden Globe-nominated actress

00:00:03.970 --> 00:00:06.573
who produces the new show
"Cruel Summer,"

00:00:06.573 --> 00:00:09.308
which airs Tuesdays
at 10:00 p.m. on Freeform

00:00:09.308 --> 00:00:11.176
and on Hulu the next day.

00:00:11.176 --> 00:00:14.480
Please welcome Jessica Biel.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:14.480 --> 00:00:16.449
Ah, I've been
looking forward to this.

00:00:16.449 --> 00:00:20.019
Yes! Jessica!
-Jimmy!

00:00:20.019 --> 00:00:21.955
-Jess, I've been
looking forward to this.

00:00:21.955 --> 00:00:24.624
I cannot wait
to talk about this project.

00:00:24.624 --> 00:00:26.860
You look fantastic.
It's great to see you.

00:00:26.860 --> 00:00:28.261
How are you?
How's the fam?

00:00:28.261 --> 00:00:30.263
How are the boys?

00:00:30.263 --> 00:00:31.631
-Oh, they're good.

00:00:31.631 --> 00:00:34.534
The family is big.

00:00:34.534 --> 00:00:36.970
They're getting big so fast.
It's so weird.

00:00:36.970 --> 00:00:38.905
They're so cute.

00:00:38.905 --> 00:00:40.639
They're really cute.
They're stinking cute.

00:00:40.639 --> 00:00:44.377
-The last time you FaceTimed me
after you had the baby,

00:00:44.377 --> 00:00:45.611
immediately after
you had the baby,

00:00:45.611 --> 00:00:48.280
and he started
doing a bit for me.

00:00:48.280 --> 00:00:49.749
He was doing comedy.

00:00:49.749 --> 00:00:52.852
-He did.
It was amazing.

00:00:52.852 --> 00:00:55.455
He was in that little --

00:00:55.455 --> 00:00:57.724
I don't know,
those weird plastic cribs

00:00:57.724 --> 00:00:59.358
that they have
in the hospital rooms.

00:00:59.358 --> 00:01:01.160
And he's laying right next to me
in the bed.

00:01:01.160 --> 00:01:02.562
-He's so cute.

00:01:02.562 --> 00:01:04.530
-But he was asleep,
and he just rolled over

00:01:04.530 --> 00:01:08.501
and he just pressed his nose
up against the glass like this.

00:01:08.501 --> 00:01:10.903
-I was like, "Dude,
that's a classic bit."

00:01:10.903 --> 00:01:13.873
He's doing the classic bit.
I loved it.

00:01:13.873 --> 00:01:15.808
Is Silas --
Are they loving each other?

00:01:15.808 --> 00:01:18.110
Are they besties?

00:01:18.110 --> 00:01:19.446
-I think they are.
-Yeah.

00:01:19.446 --> 00:01:21.213
-I really do.
And I really was worried.

00:01:21.213 --> 00:01:23.516
You know, you just never know
what's going to happen

00:01:23.516 --> 00:01:25.952
and how your older one is gonna
feel about the little one.

00:01:25.952 --> 00:01:29.755
And, man, they just think
each other are so funny.

00:01:29.755 --> 00:01:32.925
And it's so amazing to watch.

00:01:32.925 --> 00:01:34.493
It's so cute.

00:01:34.493 --> 00:01:35.894
-Do they, like,
kind of freak out

00:01:35.894 --> 00:01:37.730
because their dad
is in "Trolls,"

00:01:37.730 --> 00:01:38.898
their mom was in "Pete the Cat"?

00:01:38.898 --> 00:01:40.566
They hear these voices
and they go, like,

00:01:40.566 --> 00:01:42.301
"Wait, what's going on?"

00:01:42.301 --> 00:01:44.737
Do they understand
what you guys do?

00:01:44.737 --> 00:01:46.705
-Well, Silas does.

00:01:46.705 --> 00:01:49.875
Definitely with Justin
because of Branch.

00:01:49.875 --> 00:01:51.544
That for sure
and also his music.

00:01:51.544 --> 00:01:53.579
Whenever he hears Daddy's song,
he'll go,

00:01:53.579 --> 00:01:55.681
"Oh, yeah, that's Dad,
that's Dad."

00:01:55.681 --> 00:01:58.584
Like, "No big deal.
Yeah, whatever."

00:01:58.584 --> 00:02:01.053
But the funny thing
about "Pete the Cat"

00:02:01.053 --> 00:02:03.623
is I tried to get him
to watch the show.

00:02:03.623 --> 00:02:05.324
He will not watch the show.

00:02:05.324 --> 00:02:06.826
And yet he says,
"Hey, Mom, hey, Mom,

00:02:06.826 --> 00:02:09.362
do one of those voices
from the show."

00:02:09.362 --> 00:02:10.997
And I'm like,
"You've never seen the show.

00:02:10.997 --> 00:02:12.298
You don't even know --"

00:02:12.298 --> 00:02:14.233
He's just like, "Just do it,
Mom, just do it, Mom."

00:02:14.233 --> 00:02:15.434
And so I'll, like,
do one of the voices.

00:02:15.434 --> 00:02:17.170
"Okay, cool, Mom, cool."

00:02:17.170 --> 00:02:18.604
-[ Laughs ]

00:02:18.604 --> 00:02:20.473
Look, we've known each other
for a long time,

00:02:20.473 --> 00:02:23.176
and I just was wondering if
I could just bring up a subject

00:02:23.176 --> 00:02:25.879
and you could tell everyone
these stories that I've known,

00:02:25.879 --> 00:02:27.613
if you don't mind
telling a couple stories.

00:02:27.613 --> 00:02:29.181
-Yes, yes, let's do it.

00:02:29.181 --> 00:02:32.084
-Do you remember
selling spa water?

00:02:32.084 --> 00:02:33.752
-Oh, yeah.

00:02:33.752 --> 00:02:34.687
-Yeah.
-Yes, I do.

00:02:34.687 --> 00:02:36.789
-You scammed the neighborhood.

00:02:36.789 --> 00:02:38.224
-Yeah, we scammed
the neighborhood.

00:02:38.224 --> 00:02:41.594
My brother and I in Colorado,
when we were, I don't know,

00:02:41.594 --> 00:02:44.897
9 and 6 or 8 and 5,
something like that.

00:02:44.897 --> 00:02:46.899
We were in the tub
taking a bath,

00:02:46.899 --> 00:02:49.669
and we just dumped
everything we had --

00:02:49.669 --> 00:02:51.838
shampoo, conditioner, body wash,

00:02:51.838 --> 00:02:56.109
bath bomb, salt, foamy whatever.

00:02:56.109 --> 00:02:58.378
We probably peed in there,
I'm sure.

00:02:58.378 --> 00:03:02.248
And then we just -- we poured it
all into plastic bottles

00:03:02.248 --> 00:03:04.417
and we called it spa water

00:03:04.417 --> 00:03:06.419
and we sold it
around the cul-de-sac.

00:03:06.419 --> 00:03:07.487
[ Laughter ]

00:03:07.487 --> 00:03:09.189
-And what were people
supposed to do

00:03:09.189 --> 00:03:11.491
with spa water
once they received it?

00:03:11.491 --> 00:03:13.125
-See, now, that's the thing.

00:03:13.125 --> 00:03:14.694
Were you supposed to drink it

00:03:14.694 --> 00:03:16.829
like a cucumber water
from the spa,

00:03:16.829 --> 00:03:20.232
or were you supposed to do,
like, a refreshing spritz?

00:03:20.232 --> 00:03:22.568
I think we were going
for a spritz

00:03:22.568 --> 00:03:25.104
and not an actual ingestion,
but I don't really know.

00:03:25.104 --> 00:03:28.174
-A spritz. You were not going
for a spritz at 6 years old.

00:03:28.174 --> 00:03:30.643
Please.
Give me a break.

00:03:30.643 --> 00:03:32.611
Can you also tell the story

00:03:32.611 --> 00:03:34.780
about when you
first became famous

00:03:34.780 --> 00:03:36.582
and someone came up to you
for the first time

00:03:36.582 --> 00:03:38.284
and asked you
for your autograph?

00:03:38.284 --> 00:03:39.418
I love this.

00:03:39.418 --> 00:03:40.853
-Oh, yeah.

00:03:40.853 --> 00:03:43.522
I was so embarrassed, Jimmy.
I didn't even know what to do.

00:03:43.522 --> 00:03:46.158
This cute little girl came up,
and she said,

00:03:46.158 --> 00:03:48.294
"I love you in "7th Heaven.
I love the show.

00:03:48.294 --> 00:03:51.697
I'm a big fan.
Can I have your autograph?"

00:03:51.697 --> 00:03:54.466
And I was like,
"Only if I can have yours."

00:03:54.466 --> 00:03:58.604
She was like..."Okay."

00:03:58.604 --> 00:04:00.840
-I love that you got
her autograph, as well.

00:04:00.840 --> 00:04:02.708
I love that.
That's my favorite.

00:04:02.708 --> 00:04:04.710
I want to talk to you
about "Cruel Summer."

00:04:04.710 --> 00:04:06.913
I don't want to know
any spoilers,

00:04:06.913 --> 00:04:08.547
but I'm loving the show.
-Okay.

00:04:08.547 --> 00:04:10.683
-Everyone's talking about it.

00:04:10.683 --> 00:04:12.585
So, can we explain
what this is about?

00:04:12.585 --> 00:04:14.086
Or do you want me to explain it?

00:04:14.086 --> 00:04:17.556
-Yes, a young girl goes missing
in this small Texas community,

00:04:17.556 --> 00:04:21.194
and one of the other students
in the school

00:04:21.194 --> 00:04:25.498
gets wrapped up
in this whole thing,

00:04:25.498 --> 00:04:29.902
and it changes these
young women's lives forever.

00:04:29.902 --> 00:04:33.839
And it ricochets through
the entire community.

00:04:33.839 --> 00:04:35.341
-It is so good.

00:04:35.341 --> 00:04:37.509
Every single episode is like
another going like,

00:04:37.509 --> 00:04:39.145
"Wait, what?"
So this girl goes missing.

00:04:39.145 --> 00:04:42.915
This other girl kind of takes
her place kind of in high school

00:04:42.915 --> 00:04:45.317
and starts dating her boyfriend.

00:04:45.317 --> 00:04:48.955
Then the girl's maybe
or maybe not missing,

00:04:48.955 --> 00:04:51.790
and maybe she goes, "You know,
you were there, maybe?"

00:04:51.790 --> 00:04:53.692
And she goes,
"You know something,

00:04:53.692 --> 00:04:57.763
and you didn't say anything
about when I went missing."

00:04:57.763 --> 00:05:02.101
-Right, and the whole show
is like dual perspective.

00:05:02.101 --> 00:05:04.570
Who do you believe?
Who's telling the truth?

00:05:04.570 --> 00:05:07.573
Who's lying?
-Yes. No, we don't know.

00:05:07.573 --> 00:05:11.544
-I mean, my perception is mine,
and your reality is yours.

00:05:11.544 --> 00:05:14.012
And the truth lies somewhere
in the middle, probably.

00:05:14.012 --> 00:05:15.848
-You have a good eye
for shows like this.

00:05:15.848 --> 00:05:17.783
How do you do it?
Do you just read these scripts

00:05:17.783 --> 00:05:20.653
and you go,
"Oh, this is the one"?

00:05:20.653 --> 00:05:22.488
-I think I just look
for something

00:05:22.488 --> 00:05:25.590
that I am curious
about the mystery,

00:05:25.590 --> 00:05:28.461
I don't know the answers,

00:05:28.461 --> 00:05:32.165
where I'm like, "Ooh, I don't
know where this is going to go."

00:05:32.165 --> 00:05:34.733
-Yeah.
-And I want to be in the show.

00:05:34.733 --> 00:05:38.471
If I want to be in the show even
if I'm too old for the show,

00:05:38.471 --> 00:05:41.573
like this one, then I feel like
it's probably a good one.

00:05:41.573 --> 00:05:42.575
-Yeah, it's a great one.

